VALUES ('37bf30b5-13a2-56f3-9272-fa8250e996b9', '8290f4d8-d897-5134-812e-17ef866ba8de', 1, $json${"prompt":"**Jump Game** (LeetCode 55 — Day 18, Greedy)\n\nEach array element is your maximum jump length from that index, starting at\nindex 0. Print `true` if the last index is reachable, else `false`. The\ngreedy insight: track the furthest reachable index in one O(n) pass — no DP\nneeded.\n\n**Input:** one line of space-separated non-negative integers.\n**Output:** `true` or `false`.\n","languages":["python","javascript"],"starter_code":{"javascript":"const nums = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(0, \"utf8\").trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\n\nfunction canJump(nums) {\n  // Return true when the last index is reachable from index 0.\n}\n\nconsole.log(canJump(nums) ? \"true\" : \"false\");\n","python":"import sys\n\ndef can_jump(nums):\n    # Return True when the last index is reachable from index 0.\n    raise NotImplementedError\n\ndef main():\n    nums = list(map(int, sys.stdin.read().split()))\n    print(\"true\" if can_jump(nums) else \"false\")\n\nmain()\n"},"time_limit_ms":2000,"memory_limit_kb":262144,"test_cases":[{"id":"t1","stdin":"2 3 1 1 4","expected":"true","hidden":false,"weight":1},{"id":"t2","stdin":"3 2 1 0 4","expected":"false","hidden":false,"weight":1},{"id":"t3","stdin":"0","expected":"true","hidden":true,"weight":1},{"id":"t4","stdin":"1 0 1","expected":"false","hidden":true,"weight":1}]}$json$::jsonb, '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000012')
